  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Adopting this approach is a swift action. While you maintain this approach, whenever you use a Performance sphere ability, you can attempt a Perform check associated with the sphere ability’s package as if it were an impressive display of skill as a swift or immediate action.</p>\n<p>Additionally, whenever you use a Performance sphere ability, you can choose to have it be covert, making its existence and effects difficult to identify except to its target(s). Attempt an associated Perform check; observers must attempt a Perception or Sense Motive check against your Perform check result to realize you used a Performance sphere ability.</p>\n<p>Finally, you regain 1 use of skill leverage whenever you would gain the attention of an important individual through your performance, or when you inspire or deter someone from pursuing a motivation through your performance (up to GM discretion).</p>\n<p>Once you do, you cannot regain skill leverage that way until you regain it in a different manner.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/performance#toc17\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
